Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the USBTMC driver failing to verify the presence of required bulk-in and bulk-out endpoints, which could lead to the driver using uninitialized memory for these endpoint addresses. This oversight could result in undefined behavior, including potential crashes or incorrect operation, especially when the driver attempted to allocate and submit interrupt URBs based on these uninitialized values.

